              <name>SOC4</name>
              <description>SOC4 (Start of Conversion) overflow flag\nThis indicates an SOC4 interrupt was generated while an existing SOC4 interrupt was already pending. This overflow flag can&apos;t stop SOC4 interrupts from being processing. It just show that a trigger was missed. </description>
              <bitRange>[4:4]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
